ACORN 1.0 IWML 1.0
Features.Markdown.Index
  Data[]
    Data:Users https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users
  Styles[]
    css Index.css
  SimpleStack
    Header 2|IntraWeb Markdown
    Text
      Text:
        [off]IntraWeb 17 supports inline markdown which is also expandable. There are several built in tags, and you can add  your own ones by registering a handler, or even a local one using a function.
        To use markdown, wrap the target in []. The full syntax is [tag(params):value].
        Here we use them with Text controls but many other controls support IntraWeb Markdown also.
    SimpleStack
      Header 3|HTML
      Text [html]No Markdown using HTML tag [Hello]
      Text [html]HTML <b>bold</b><span style="Visibility: inline-block; width: 30pt"></span>Space 30

      Header 3|HTML(style)
      Text [html]<span class="bluebg">Blue Background from CSS</span> No more CSS here...
      Text [html(bluebg)]Blue Background from CSS. Everything is CSS.
      Text [html(bluebg):Blue Background from CSS] No more CSS here...

      Header 3|Off
      Text [off]No Markdown using OFF tag [Hello]
      Text [off]Text with special[]
      Text [off]Text with special]

      Header 3|Space(30)
      Text Text with[space(30)]Space 30

      Header 3|B / I
      Text [b:Bold] and [i:Italic]

      Header 3|EOL
      Text Embedded EOL[eol]After EOL

      Header 3|Atozed-Uppercase
      Text You can define your own markdown. This is a custom markdown tag defined in the accompanying code file.
      Text [Atozed-UpperCase:Hello]
      Text [Atozed-UpperCase]Hello

      Header 3|Data Binding
      Text Data from the JSON data set in the URL inside the IWML file. We haven't moved the cusror, so it shows data from the first row. Users in the data section points to:
      Link https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users|https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users
      Text [off] The tag used below is [=.Users.name]
      Text Name: [=.Users.name]

      Header 3|this - Code Property Binding
      Text These values are properties declared in the code file.
      Text MagicNo: [=this.MagicNo]
      Text Message: [=this.Message] [=this.MagicNo]
      Text If you change the values in code, the bindings update automatically. Push this button to see.
      Button:ThisButton Change

      Header 3|More Bindings
      Text [off]In addition to Markdown tags, any binding can also be used by using =. ie [=binding].
      Text For all data binding types beyond what is shown here, see the Data Binding demo.
      Text Bindings in markdown become readonly. To preserve two way, use data binding instead.

      Header 3|More Markdown tags
      Text Here is a complete list of Markdown tags.
      TextList:TagList